        "version": 1,
        "side": "construction",
        "payload": {
          "name": "Preserve region for location memories",
          "description": "When a message mentions a city, town, or landmark, include its unambiguous state/province/country during extraction and when enriching location memories.",
          "content": [
            "When extracting a memory from a message that names a city, town, or landmark, also record the containing state/province/country if that relation is well-known and unambiguous.",
            "When updating or enriching an existing location memory, ensure the broader administrative region is preserved alongside the specific place.",
            "Do not guess ambiguous region mappings; only add the state/province/country when the connection is certain."
          ]
        },
        "solves": "When a conversational message names a city, town, or landmark, extraction often records only that specific place and drops the containing state/province/country, so later state-level or country-level questions cannot be answered from memory. This skill ensures the broader administrative region is preserved whenever it is an unambiguous, well-known fact.",
        "related_existing_skill_ids": [
          "sk_construction_travel_location_period"
        ],
        "source_diagnosis_id": "cons_conv-42_conv-42_qa_0087",
        "source_failure_id": "cons_conv-42_conv-42_qa_0087",
        "target_first_break": null,
        "parent_version_id": null,
        "status": "staged",
        "created_at": "2026-08-02T14:22:33Z"
      },
      {
        "candidate_id": "cand_construction_7e913ad2e93a",
        "skill_id": "sk_construction_a112a5a855",
        "version": 1,
        "side": "construction",
        "payload": {
          "name": "Resolve relative vacation times and locations",
          "description": "When a message describes a trip, vacation, or photo with a relative time like 'last summer' and a place, resolve the time from the message/session timestamp and extract the visit as an event with a location.",
          "content": [
            "During extraction, if a message mentions travel, vacation, or a photo taken on a trip with a relative time phrase (e.g., 'last summer', 'last winter', 'a few months ago') and a place, do not skip it for lacking an explicit date.",
            "Resolve the relative time using the message/session timestamp to determine the concrete season or period, and infer the country when the mentioned city is unambiguous.",
            "Create an event memory for the person's visit to that location during the resolved time, linked to the source message, including the specific place name and country when inferable."
          ]
        },
        "solves": "Construction often misses durable facts when a user mentions a vacation or photo with a relative time phrase (e.g., 'last summer') and a city, but no explicit date or country. The diagnosed cause was that no candidate was generated from such a message, leaving the place and time unrecorded. This rule applies whenever extraction must resolve relative time from the message timestamp and create a dated location event.",
        "related_existing_skill_ids": [
          "sk_construction_travel_location_period"
        ],
